# Every text file is committed and checked out with LF on every system,
# whatever core.autocrlf a host sets; git tells text from binary by content.
# The code beside the data below (the fixtures' code, the vendored
# library's CMake and README) stays so, under B32.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The data whose bytes a case or a pin reads by digest or byte for byte,
# each named with what reads it: kept byte for byte, never normalized,
# whatever their content.
# The fixtures and the digest vectors: each compiled into the cases as its
# bytes (tests/support/fixtures/CMakeLists.txt) and parsed strictly; each
# vector pins its expected bytes.
tests/fixtures/entries.json -text
tests/vectors/ids.json -text
# The fuzz targets' regression corpora: inputs by their bytes, each named
# by its SHA-1 and compiled in as its bytes (tests/fuzz/CMakeLists.txt);
# these directories hold such inputs alone. A pattern ends in /** because
# an attributes pattern does not reach into a directory.
tests/fuzz/digest/regress/** -text
tests/fuzz/entry/regress/** -text
# The vendored SQLite amalgamation, as its upstream ships it: each file's
# SHA-256 pinned in CMakeLists.txt and checked on every configure.
third_party/sqlite/sqlite3.c -text
third_party/sqlite/sqlite3.h -text

# Windows' command interpreter reads its scripts with CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
